---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
GZIP Decompression:
Purpose: Reverses the compression process, expanding the GZIP-compressed data back to its original format.

Algorithm: Uses the same DEFLATE algorithm as GZIP compression, but in reverse.
Benefits: Ensures that the original message content is restored accurately.

How it works:
Reads the compressed data, identifies the short codes and their corresponding references.
Uses the dictionary to reconstruct the original data by expanding the short codes back to their corresponding sequences of bytes.
Example in CPI: The GZIP Decoder can be used to uncompress a GZIP-compressed message during an integration flow.

